 fixture's verdict moves:                                                       
 the change is confined to the documents named above. No requirement row        
 changed, so no record that read                                                
 `OK` can read `FAILED`.                                                        
                                                                                
 ## 3. What changed and what did not                                            
                                                                                
 The header of `SPEC.md` names the release and the field table's example        
 follows it; nothing else in that                                               
 document moved. `CHANGELOG.md` carries the release's entry, which says no      
 requirement changed.                                                           
 `CONTRIBUTING.md` stops naming the earlier release by a bare version token —   
 the sentence still says                                                        
 which release shipped without a record and where its note is kept — and its    
 Releases section carries the                                                   
 cadence amendment. `README.md` states the new status, and both files under the 
 minimal example declare                                                        
 the release. We deliberately left the verifier, the counting tool, the schema, 
 the fixtures and                                                               
 everything under `record/` untouched.                                          
                                                                                
 ## 4. Where to look hardest                                                    
                                                                                
