The failure is in measure_cadence: it looks for the Owner's amendment verbatim  
inside CONTRIBUTING.md's ## Releases section, and my earlier sentence began with
a capital A (A release that changes no requirement…) while the needle is        
lowercase (a release that changes no requirement…). carried_verbatim compares   
the words as a sequence, so the capital breaks the match.                       

The fix is to embed the amendment's exact words mid-sentence (lowercased) so it 
is carried verbatim, on one line, inside the Releases section:                  

